# Windows Defender Firewall — Remove/Disable for Privilege Escalation

Class date: 31/07/2026 • Two-part practical demo on Windows Server 2025 (VM: Windows-Server-Privilege-Esc).

**Why: During privilege escalation, Windows Defender (real-time protection + Microsoft Defender Antivirus) will detect and delete your exploit/payload. Before running any exploit, Defender must be disabled or removed.**

---

## Part 1 — Video: 18.Window-defender-remove.mkv (Hindi Explanation)

## Video 1: 18.Window-defender-remove.mkv — Spoken Explanation (Hindi)

### Video Overview

Hindi explanation of how to **remove/disable Windows Defender** so that exploits

and payloads are not blocked during penetration testing / privilege escalation.

#### Why disable Defender

- Jab aap privilege escalation mein exploit chalate hain, **Windows Defender pakad ke delete kar deta hai**
- `nc.exe` (netcat), `msfvenom` payloads, exploit files — sabko Defender detect karke remove kar deta hai
- Isliye pehle Defender ko disable/remove karna zaroori hai
- Penetration testing lab mein antivirus bypass karne ka sabse bada challenge yahi hai

#### Tamper Protection — sabse pehle

- **Tamper Protection ON** hone par aap Defender ko disable nahi kar sakte
- Jab tak Tamper Protection on hai, tab tak koi bhi change allow nahi karega
- Navigation: **Windows Security → Virus & threat protection → Manage settings → Tamper Protection**
- Tamper Protection ko OFF karna zaroori hai, warna baaki sab kaam nahi chalega

### Method 1 — Group Policy Registry Keys se Disable

PowerShell (as Administrator) se:

```powershell
Set-ItemProperty -Path "HKLM:\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows Defender" -Name "DisableAntiSpyware" -Value 1 -Type DWord
Set-ItemProperty -Path "HKLM:\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows Defender\Real-Time Protection" -Name "DisableOnAccessProtection" -Value 1 -Type DWord
```

### Method 2 — Stop & Disable Services

```powershell
Stop-Service -Name "WinDefend" -Force
Stop-Service -Name "WdNisSvc" -Force
Stop-Service -Name "Sense" -Force
```

Services restart hone par phir start ho jati hain, isliye startup type bhi disable karo:

```powershell
Set-Service -Name "WinDefend" -StartupType Disabled
Set-Service -Name "WdNisSvc" -StartupType Disabled
Set-Service -Name "Sense" -StartupType Disabled
```

### Method 3 — Offline (Image) se Defender Package Remove

- Group policy turn off → stop & disable services → **remove Defender package from the image**
- Online nahi kar sakte, offline image mein jake package remove karna hota hai
- `DISM` command se offline image mein Defender package uninstall

### UAC aur Safe Mode

- **UAC** check karo — kabhi kabhi UAC bhi block kar deta hai
- `cmd` ko **Run as Administrator** se chalao
- Kuch commands **Safe Mode** mein chalani padti hain (services block hain)
- WinRE (Windows Recovery Environment) se bhi commands chala sakte ho

### Verification (EICAR Test File)

- EICAR test file download karke verify karo ki Defender off hai ya nahi
- `malware test file` / EICAR — agar download ho gaya aur **no detection** = Defender off
- Check: `Settings → Security & Privacy → Windows Security` → koi detection nahi honi chahiye
- `Get-Service -Name WinDefend, WdNisSvc, Sense | Select-Object Name, Status, StartType`

### Important Points (Batch ka schedule)

- Kal exam hai, toh **system format mat karna** aur Kali reload mat karna
- Controller banane mein lagta hai ~1 ghanta (minimum 1.5–2 ghante)
- **nc.exe** aur **msfvenom payloads** pehle se rakh lo
- Iska matlab nahi ki antivirus hone se kaam nahi chalega — test environment mein jab tak

bypass nahi karte, tab tak antivirus active rahega

- Antivirus bypass ke liye: payload generation + obfuscation + Defender disable

