### Part 2 — Stop and Disable Defender Services (Method 2)

Microsoft Defender services are protected by Windows. These commands typically require:

- Safe Mode
- Local SYSTEM privileges (for example, PsExec)
- Windows Recovery Environment (WinRE)

#### 2.1 Stop Defender Services

```powershell
Stop-Service -Name "WinDefend" -Force
Stop-Service -Name "WdNisSvc" -Force
Stop-Service -Name "Sense" -Force
```

Note: On this lab, services were already removed → "Cannot find any service with service name 'WinDefend'" errors are expected.

#### 2.2 Disable Service Startup

```powershell
Set-Service -Name "WinDefend" -StartupType Disabled
Set-Service -Name "WdNisSvc" -StartupType Disabled
Set-Service -Name "Sense" -StartupType Disabled
```

#### 2.3 Disable Services via Registry

A reboot is required.

