### Part 4 — Disable Defender Core Services via Registry (Notepad script)

Created a PowerShell script `1.ps1` in `C:\Users\Administrator\Documents\`:

```powershell
# 1. Disable Microsoft Defender Core Services
$services = @("WinDefend", "WdNisSvc", "Sense", "WdBoot", "WdFilter", "SecurityHealthService")
foreach ($service in $services) {
    $path = "HKLM:\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\$service"
    if (Test-Path $path) {
        Set-ItemProperty -Path $path -Name "Start" -Value 4 -Type DWord
        Write-Host "Disabled service: $service" -ForegroundColor Green
    }
}

# 2. Enforce Group Policy Registry Keys to Disable Defender
$gpPath = "HKLM:\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows Defender"
```

Ran it in Safe Mode:

```powershell
cd C:\Users\Administrator\Documents
.\1.ps1
```

Output: `Disabled service: WinDefend`

