### Part 6 — Verification after reboot

- After rebooting into normal Windows Server 2025, checked services:

```powershell
Get-Service -Name WinDefend, WdNisSvc, Sense | Select-Object Name, Status, StartType
```

→ Services not found (already removed/disabled — expected on this lab)

#### 6.1 EICAR test to confirm Defender is OFF

- Downloaded **EICAR test file** from eicar.org (anti-malware test file, `eicar.com` / `eicar.com.txt`)
- In normal state, Microsoft Defender blocked it ("eicar_com.zip was blocked as unsafe")
- After disable, **eicar.com downloaded successfully and was NOT blocked** → confirms Defender is fully disabled

#### 6.2 Windows Security status

- Opened `Settings → Privacy & security → Windows Security`
- Virus & threat protection / Firewall & network protection pages show no active threats
- Defender no longer interfering

