## Quick Command Cheat-Sheet

```powershell
# 1. Disable via Group Policy registry keys (PowerShell as Admin)
Set-ItemProperty -Path "HKLM:\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows Defender" -Name "DisableAntiSpyware" -Value 1 -Type DWord
Set-ItemProperty -Path "HKLM:\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows Defender\Real-Time Protection" -Name "DisableOnAccessProtection" -Value 1 -Type DWord

# 2. Stop Defender services (needs Safe Mode / SYSTEM / WinRE)
Stop-Service -Name "WinDefend" -Force
Stop-Service -Name "WdNisSvc" -Force
Stop-Service -Name "Sense" -Force

# 3. Disable service startup
Set-Service -Name "WinDefend" -StartupType Disabled
Set-Service -Name "WdNisSvc" -StartupType Disabled
Set-Service -Name "Sense" -StartupType Disabled

# 4. SYSTEM shell via PsExec (Sysinternals)
C:\Users\Administrator\Downloads\PSTools\PsExec64.exe -i -s powershell.exe
whoami   # -> nt authority\system
```

Note: Beginning with Windows 10 Version 2004, the DisableAntiSpyware registry value is ignored on most consumer editions unless a supported third-party antivirus product is registered. For servers, disabling the services + registry Start=4 (via Safe Mode / Hiren's BootCD PE / offline SYSTEM hive) is the reliable method.

